.TH BREWMASTER 1 "2026-06-14" "brewmaster 0.6.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
brewmaster \- selective Homebrew package upgrades by semver bump level
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B brewmaster
[\fBupgrade\fR] [\fIpackages...\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B brewmaster snapshot
{\fBsave\fR|\fBlist\fR|\fBdiff\fR|\fBrestore\fR|\fBdelete\fR}
[\fIref\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B brewmaster deps show
[\fIpackage\fR]
.br
.B brewmaster profile
{\fBlist\fR|\fBcreate\fR|\fBedit\fR|\fBdiff\fR|\fBvalidate\fR} [\fIargs\fR]
.br
.B brewmaster cleanup
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR|\fB\-\-interactive\fR|\fB\-\-force\fR]
.br
.B brewmaster why
\fIpackage\fR
.br
.B brewmaster bloat
.br
.B brewmaster log
[\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B brewmaster report
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B brewmaster
upgrades only what you decide \(em patch, minor, or major \(em nothing more.
It classifies every outdated package by its semantic-versioning bump, gates
the upgrade by the requested level, and understands
.I why
a package exists on your machine before touching it.
.PP
brewmaster is deterministic: no AI, no guessing, no network calls beyond
.BR brew (1)
itself.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Upgrade (default command)
.TP
.BI upgrade " [packages...]"
Selective upgrade by semver bump level. Pass package names to limit the
upgrade to those, e.g.
.IR "brewmaster upgrade git node --minor" .
.SS Dependency risk
.TP
.BI "deps show " "[package]"
Show dependency risk for one package, or list all outdated packages sorted
by risk score.
.SS Snapshot & rollback
.TP
.B snapshot save
Save current Homebrew state to a snapshot.
.TP
.B snapshot list
List all saved snapshots.
.TP
.BI "snapshot diff " "[index|path]"
Show packages changed since a snapshot.
.TP
.BI "snapshot restore " "[index|path]"
Restore packages to a snapshot state.
.TP
.BI "snapshot delete " "[index|path]"
Delete a snapshot.
.SS Profiles
.TP
.B profile list
List configured profiles.
.TP
.B profile create
Interactive wizard to add a new profile.
.TP
.BI "profile edit " "[name]"
Open
.I profiles.toml
in
.BR $EDITOR .
.TP
.BI "profile diff " "a b"
Compare include lists between two profiles.
.TP
.B profile validate
Check
.I profiles.toml
for errors.
.SS Cleanup & intent
.TP
.B cleanup
Report orphan, stale, and pinned-old formulae (read-only by default).
.TP
.BI why " package"
Explain why a formula is installed: dependents, install date, and a
last-access heuristic.
.TP
.B bloat
Summary of installed package counts and estimated disk reclaim from
cleanup candidates.
.SS Audit log & reports
.TP
.B log
Show recent audit log entries (last 20 by default).
.TP
.B report
Machine health summary: upgrades, cleanups, snapshots, orphans, and risk
trend.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Level (mutually exclusive; default: patch)
.TP
.B \-\-patch
Apply patch bumps only (default).
.TP
.B \-\-minor
Apply minor bumps only.
.TP
.B \-\-major
Apply major bumps only.
.TP
.BI \-\-level= patch|minor|major
Same as the flags above (also accepted as
.IR "--level minor" ).
.SS Upgrade flags
.TP
.B \-\-or\-lower
Make the level inclusive (e.g.
.B \-\-minor
=> minor+patch;
.B \-\-major
=> all).
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-date
Treat date versions
.RI ( YYYY.MM.DD / YYYY-MM-DD ...)
as semver-like. Default: off.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Show the plan without executing.
.TP
.B \-\-formulae
Formulae only (skip casks).
.TP
.B \-\-casks
Casks only (skip formulae).
.TP
.BI \-\-profile= NAME
Filter and level from a named profile (see
.B FILES
for
.IR profiles.toml ).
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interactive
fzf multi-select among upgrade candidates (requires
.BR fzf ).
.SS Dependency risk flags (apply to upgrade)
.TP
.B \-\-check\-deps
Risk-score each upgrade candidate; skip HIGH-risk, warn on MEDIUM.
.TP
.BI \-\-risk\-threshold= N
HIGH-risk cutoff (default: 7; range 0\-10).
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Auto-confirm MEDIUM-risk packages (no prompt).
.SS Snapshot flags
.TP
.BI \-\-label= TEXT
Label for
.BR "snapshot save" .
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Show plan without executing, for
.BR "snapshot restore" .
.TP
.B \-\-force
Skip the y/N confirmation for
.BR "snapshot delete" .
.SS Cleanup flags
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Read-only report (also the default with no flags).
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interactive
fzf multi-select packages to remove (requires
.BR fzf ).
.TP
.B \-\-force
Auto-remove orphans with cleanup score >= 7, no confirmation.
.SS Log flags
.TP
.BI \-\-package= NAME
Filter entries by package name.
.TP
.BI \-\-action= ACTION
Filter by action:
.BR upgrade ", " cleanup ", or " snapshot .
.TP
.BI \-\-since= Nd|Nh|Nw
Only entries within this time window (default unit: days).
.TP
.BI \-\-format= table|json|csv
Output format (default: table).
.SS General
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
More detailed output.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the full reference (there is no per-subcommand
.BR \-\-help ).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B brewmaster
Apply patch-level upgrades (the default).
.TP
.B brewmaster --minor --or-lower
Apply minor and patch upgrades.
.TP
.B brewmaster upgrade git node --minor
Limit the upgrade to specific packages.
.TP
.B brewmaster snapshot save --label="before-work-upgrade"
Save the current package state before a risky upgrade.
.TP
.B brewmaster snapshot restore 1 --dry-run
Preview what restoring the most recent snapshot would do.
.TP
.B brewmaster cleanup --interactive
Pick orphaned packages to remove via fzf.
.TP
.B brewmaster why git
Explain why
.B git
is installed.
.TP
.B brewmaster log --action=cleanup --since=30d
Show cleanup actions from the last 30 days.
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
.BR \-\-patch / \-\-minor / \-\-major
and
.B \-\-level=X
are equivalent; pick whichever reads better in scripts vs interactively.
.IP \(bu 2
.B \-\-force
has different effects per command:
.B "snapshot delete"
skips a y/N confirmation;
.B cleanup
auto-removes high-confidence orphans.
.IP \(bu 2
Two different 0\-10 scores, opposite directions: the
.I risk score
.RB ( "deps" ", " \-\-check\-deps )
\(em higher means more dangerous to upgrade (HIGH >= threshold, default 7;
MEDIUM 4\-6; LOW 0\-3) \(em and the
.I cleanup score
.RB ( "cleanup" ", " why )
\(em higher means safer to remove.
.IP \(bu 2
Pre-release
.RI ( -rc.1 )
and
.RI ( +build )
metadata are ignored during comparison (only major.minor.patch).
.IP \(bu 2
Date/timestamp versions are skipped unless
.B \-\-allow\-date
is used.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/brewmaster/snapshots/
Saved snapshots (respects
.BR XDG_DATA_HOME ).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/brewmaster/audit.log
NDJSON audit log of upgrades, cleanups, and snapshots (respects
.BR XDG_DATA_HOME ).
.TP
.I ~/.config/brewmaster/profiles.toml
Named upgrade profiles (respects
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Overrides the base directory for snapshots and the audit log. Default:
.IR ~/.local/share .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Overrides the base directory for
.IR profiles.toml .
Default:
.IR ~/.config .
.TP
.B EDITOR
Editor used by
.BR "profile edit" .
Falls back to
.BR nano .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success;
.B 1
if any upgrade, restore, or install step fails, or on usage errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR brew (1)
.SH BUGS
Report issues at
.UR https://github.com/pimlabs/brewmaster/issues
the brewmaster issue tracker
.UE .
